IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `il-interpretation-time`
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g6-nouns`
IMPORT `g6-schedule-three`
IMPORT `g6-notice-and-hearing`
IMPORT `g6-amount`

-- g6-tests-amount.l4: tests of ss.45-47.
-- Expected values were decided from the Hebrew of ss.45-47 (law.wiki lines 365-376; gazette p. 194) and
-- from Interpretation Law s.10 before any run, by hand and then cross-checked with Python's Fraction
-- arithmetic (not with the module):
--   s.45(a): one fiftieth of the fixed sanction for each month; s.45(b): an equal amount again;
--   s.47(b): the amounts are updated each 1 January by (the index known on that day / the index known on
--     1 January of the year before), rounded to the nearest multiple of NIS 10.
-- The index series below is invented for the tests (the sources give no readings, trap in section 9):
--   known on 1 Jan 2025: 100.0   known on 1 Jan 2026: 101.7   known on 1 Jan 2027: 103.4
-- so the ratios are 1.017 for 2026 and 103.4/101.7 for 2027.  Worked by hand:
--   20,000 -> 20,340 (2026) -> 20,680 (2027, as 20,340 = 200 x 101.7 and 200 x 103.4 = 20,680);
--   5,000 -> 5,085, which is HALF-WAY between 5,080 and 5,090: half up gives 5,090 (taken), half to even 5,080;
--   5,090 x 103.4/101.7 = 5,175.1 -> 5,180 with each year rounded, but 5,000 x 103.4/100.0 = 5,170 rounded once.

§ `Tests of ss 45 to 47`

§§ `Fixtures`

`an individual violator`  MEANS Person WITH `reference for the person` IS "P-IND", `kind of person` IS `an individual`
`another individual`      MEANS Person WITH `reference for the person` IS "P-OTHER", `kind of person` IS `an individual`
`a corporate violator`    MEANS Person WITH `reference for the person` IS "P-CORP", `kind of person` IS `a corporation`

`violation (1)` MEANS `work with no licence at all`
`violation (2)` MEANS `work without a licence of the kind appropriate to the system`
`violation (3)` MEANS `advertising as licensed without the licence or the kind`
`violation (4)` MEANS `installation without the tightness test of the piping`
`violation (5)` MEANS `engaging a person who had no licence at all`
`violation (6)` MEANS `engaging a person without a licence of the appropriate kind`
`violation (7)` MEANS `failing to give a document an inspector demanded`

GIVEN who IS A Person
      item IS A `Listed violation`
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A Violation
`a violation by` who `of` item `on` day MEANS
    Violation WITH `the violator` IS who
                 , `the listed violation` IS item
                 , `reference for the act` IS "act-1"
                 , `date of the act` IS day

-- Positional fields of `Previous violation`: violator, violation, date of the act, sanction imposed, convicted.
`an earlier item (1) violation on 16 March 2027, sanctioned`   MEANS `Previous violation` OF `an individual violator`, `violation (1)`, YMD 2027 3 16, TRUE,  FALSE
`an earlier item (1) violation on 16 March 2027, convicted`    MEANS `Previous violation` OF `an individual violator`, `violation (1)`, YMD 2027 3 16, FALSE, TRUE
`an earlier item (1) violation on 16 March 2027, neither`      MEANS `Previous violation` OF `an individual violator`, `violation (1)`, YMD 2027 3 16, FALSE, FALSE
`an earlier item (5) violation on 16 March 2027, sanctioned`   MEANS `Previous violation` OF `an individual violator`, `violation (5)`, YMD 2027 3 16, TRUE,  FALSE
`an earlier item (3) violation on 16 March 2027, sanctioned`   MEANS `Previous violation` OF `an individual violator`, `violation (3)`, YMD 2027 3 16, TRUE,  FALSE
`an earlier item (1) violation by another person, sanctioned`  MEANS `Previous violation` OF `another individual`, `violation (1)`, YMD 2027 3 16, TRUE,  FALSE
`an earlier item (1) violation on 29 February 2028, sanctioned` MEANS `Previous violation` OF `an individual violator`, `violation (1)`, YMD 2028 2 29, TRUE,  FALSE

`the Friday 16 and Saturday 17 March 2029 as days of rest` MEANS `Calendar of rest days` WITH `days of rest, recess or holiday` IS LIST (YMD 2029 3 16), (YMD 2029 3 17)

-- The index series: Nov 2024 100.0 (published 15 Dec 2024), Dec 2024 100.4 (15 Jan 2025), Nov 2025 101.7 (15 Dec 2025),
-- Dec 2025 101.9 (15 Jan 2026), Nov 2026 103.4 (15 Dec 2026), Dec 2026 103.6 (15 Jan 2027), and an older Oct 2024 reading 99.8.
-- Positional fields of `Price index reading`: year, month, published on, value.
`the index readings` MEANS
    LIST (`Price index reading` OF 2024, 10, YMD 2024 11 15,  99.8)
       , (`Price index reading` OF 2024, 11, YMD 2024 12 15, 100.0)
       , (`Price index reading` OF 2024, 12, YMD 2025 1 15,  100.4)
       , (`Price index reading` OF 2025, 11, YMD 2025 12 15, 101.7)
       , (`Price index reading` OF 2025, 12, YMD 2026 1 15,  101.9)
       , (`Price index reading` OF 2026, 11, YMD 2026 12 15, 103.4)
       , (`Price index reading` OF 2026, 12, YMD 2027 1 15,  103.6)

§§ `s 45(a): months of a continuing violation, three counts (fork F-MONTHS)`

-- A violation that began on 15 March 2027 and last continued on 14 June 2027:
--   months completed: month 1 ends 15 April, month 2 ends 15 May, month 3 would end 15 June, after the 14th: 2.
--   calendar months touched: March, April, May, June: 4.   after the first: 3.
#ASSERT `s 45(a) — the whole months a violation continued from` (YMD 2027 3 15) `to` (YMD 2027 6 14) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `s 45(a) — the calendar months touched by a violation from` (YMD 2027 3 15) `to` (YMD 2027 6 14) EQUALS 4
#ASSERT `s 45(a) — the calendar months touched after the first, by a violation from` (YMD 2027 3 15) `to` (YMD 2027 6 14) EQUALS 3
-- The third month completes exactly on 15 June: the last day of the period of 3 months is inside it.
#ASSERT `s 45(a) — the whole months a violation continued from` (YMD 2027 3 15) `to` (YMD 2027 6 15) EQUALS 3
-- A violation that has run 5 days has completed no month, touches one calendar month, and none after the first.
#ASSERT `s 45(a) — the whole months a violation continued from` (YMD 2027 3 15) `to` (YMD 2027 3 20) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 45(a) — the calendar months touched by a violation from` (YMD 2027 3 15) `to` (YMD 2027 3 20) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `s 45(a) — the calendar months touched after the first, by a violation from` (YMD 2027 3 15) `to` (YMD 2027 3 20) EQUALS 0
-- A violation that ended the day it began, and one that "ended" before it began.
#ASSERT `s 45(a) — the whole months a violation continued from` (YMD 2027 3 15) `to` (YMD 2027 3 15) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 45(a) — the calendar months touched by a violation from` (YMD 2027 3 15) `to` (YMD 2027 3 15) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `s 45(a) — the whole months a violation continued from` (YMD 2027 3 15) `to` (YMD 2027 3 14) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 45(a) — the calendar months touched by a violation from` (YMD 2027 3 15) `to` (YMD 2027 3 14) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 45(a) — the calendar months touched after the first, by a violation from` (YMD 2027 3 15) `to` (YMD 2027 3 14) EQUALS 0
-- A start on the 31st: month 1 ends on 28 February 2027 (IL s.10(b): the month's last day), month 2 on 31 March.
#ASSERT `s 45(a) — the whole months a violation continued from` (YMD 2027 1 31) `to` (YMD 2027 2 27) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 45(a) — the whole months a violation continued from` (YMD 2027 1 31) `to` (YMD 2027 2 28) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `s 45(a) — the whole months a violation continued from` (YMD 2027 1 31) `to` (YMD 2027 3 30) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `s 45(a) — the whole months a violation continued from` (YMD 2027 1 31) `to` (YMD 2027 3 31) EQUALS 2
-- ... and in a leap year month 1 ends on 29 February 2028.
#ASSERT `s 45(a) — the whole months a violation continued from` (YMD 2028 1 31) `to` (YMD 2028 2 28) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 45(a) — the whole months a violation continued from` (YMD 2028 1 31) `to` (YMD 2028 2 29) EQUALS 1
-- Across a year end: 15 November 2027 to 15 February 2028 is three months.
#ASSERT `s 45(a) — the whole months a violation continued from` (YMD 2027 11 15) `to` (YMD 2028 2 15) EQUALS 3

-- One fiftieth for each month: 20,000 / 50 = 400 a month; 5,000 / 50 = 100; 3,000 / 50 = 60.
#ASSERT `s 45(a) — the addition of one fiftieth of` 20_000 `for each of the months` 0 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 45(a) — the addition of one fiftieth of` 20_000 `for each of the months` 1 EQUALS 400
#ASSERT `s 45(a) — the addition of one fiftieth of` 20_000 `for each of the months` 2 EQUALS 800
#ASSERT `s 45(a) — the addition of one fiftieth of` 5_000 `for each of the months` 3 EQUALS 300
#ASSERT `s 45(a) — the addition of one fiftieth of` 3_000 `for each of the months` 1 EQUALS 60
-- Fifty months of the fixed sanction is the fixed sanction again: 50 x one fiftieth.
#ASSERT `s 45(a) — the addition of one fiftieth of` 10_000 `for each of the months` 50 EQUALS 10_000

§§ `s 45(b): the window of two years from the previous violation (kind B: no IL s.10(c)); both edges`

-- Two years after 16 March 2027: 16 March 2029, a Friday.  The last day is inside the window.
#ASSERT `s 45(b) — the last day of the two years from the previous violation` `an earlier item (1) violation on 16 March 2027, sanctioned` EQUALS YMD 2029 3 16
-- Two years after 29 February 2028: the month lacks the day, so the last day of the month, 28 February 2030.
#ASSERT `s 45(b) — the last day of the two years from the previous violation` `an earlier item (1) violation on 29 February 2028, sanctioned` EQUALS YMD 2030 2 28

#ASSERT     `s 45(b) — the violation` (`a violation by` `an individual violator` `of` `violation (1)` `on` (YMD 2029 3 16)) `is a repeat violation, given` (LIST `an earlier item (1) violation on 16 March 2027, sanctioned`)
#ASSERT NOT `s 45(b) — the violation` (`a violation by` `an individual violator` `of` `violation (1)` `on` (YMD 2029 3 17)) `is a repeat violation, given` (LIST `an earlier item (1) violation on 16 March 2027, sanctioned`)
-- The day after the previous violation is inside; the day itself is not "after" it.
#ASSERT     `s 45(b) — the violation` (`a violation by` `an individual violator` `of` `violation (1)` `on` (YMD 2027 3 17)) `is a repeat violation, given` (LIST `an earlier item (1) violation on 16 March 2027, sanctioned`)
#ASSERT NOT `s 45(b) — the violation` (`a violation by` `an individual violator` `of` `violation (1)` `on` (YMD 2027 3 16)) `is a repeat violation, given` (LIST `an earlier item (1) violation on 16 March 2027, sanctioned`)
#ASSERT NOT `s 45(b) — the violation` (`a violation by` `an individual violator` `of` `violation (1)` `on` (YMD 2027 3 15)) `is a repeat violation, given` (LIST `an earlier item (1) violation on 16 March 2027, sanctioned`)
-- The leap-day previous violation: 28 February 2030 is the last day, 1 March 2030 is outside.
#ASSERT     `s 45(b) — the violation` (`a violation by` `an individual violator` `of` `violation (1)` `on` (YMD 2030 2 28)) `is a repeat violation, given` (LIST `an earlier item (1) violation on 29 February 2028, sanctioned`)
#ASSERT NOT `s 45(b) — the violation` (`a violation by` `an individual violator` `of` `violation (1)` `on` (YMD 2030 3 1)) `is a repeat violation, given` (LIST `an earlier item (1) violation on 29 February 2028, sanctioned`)

-- What the previous violation must have ended in: a sanction or a conviction; neither is not enough.
#ASSERT     `s 45(b) — the violation` (`a violation by` `an individual violator` `of` `violation (1)` `on` (YMD 2028 6 1)) `is a repeat violation, given` (LIST `an earlier item (1) violation on 16 March 2027, convicted`)
#ASSERT NOT `s 45(b) — the violation` (`a violation by` `an individual violator` `of` `violation (1)` `on` (YMD 2028 6 1)) `is a repeat violation, given` (LIST `an earlier item (1) violation on 16 March 2027, neither`)
-- It must be the same violator's, and the same provision.
#ASSERT NOT `s 45(b) — the violation` (`a violation by` `an individual violator` `of` `violation (1)` `on` (YMD 2028 6 1)) `is a repeat violation, given` (LIST `an earlier item (1) violation by another person, sanctioned`)
#ASSERT NOT `s 45(b) — the violation` (`a violation by` `an individual violator` `of` `violation (4)` `on` (YMD 2028 6 1)) `is a repeat violation, given` (LIST `an earlier item (3) violation on 16 March 2027, sanctioned`)
-- No previous violation at all.
#ASSERT NOT `s 45(b) — the violation` (`a violation by` `an individual violator` `of` `violation (1)` `on` (YMD 2028 6 1)) `is a repeat violation, given` EMPTY
-- Any one of several previous violations will do.
#ASSERT     `s 45(b) — the violation` (`a violation by` `an individual violator` `of` `violation (1)` `on` (YMD 2028 6 1)) `is a repeat violation, given` (LIST `an earlier item (1) violation on 16 March 2027, neither`, `an earlier item (1) violation on 16 March 2027, sanctioned`)

-- "The same provision" (F-SAME): items (1) and (2) both contravene s.3(a), items (5) and (6) both s.18(a).
-- Read by provision, an item (1) violation followed by an item (2) violation is a repeat; read by item, it is not.
#ASSERT     `s 45(b) — the violation` (`a violation by` `an individual violator` `of` `violation (2)` `on` (YMD 2028 6 1)) `is a repeat violation, given` (LIST `an earlier item (1) violation on 16 March 2027, sanctioned`)
#ASSERT NOT `s 45(b) — the previous violation, read by Third Schedule item, makes the violation a repeat violation` (`a violation by` `an individual violator` `of` `violation (2)` `on` (YMD 2028 6 1)) `an earlier item (1) violation on 16 March 2027, sanctioned`
#ASSERT     `s 45(b) — the violation` (`a violation by` `an individual violator` `of` `violation (6)` `on` (YMD 2028 6 1)) `is a repeat violation, given` (LIST `an earlier item (5) violation on 16 March 2027, sanctioned`)
#ASSERT NOT `s 45(b) — the previous violation, read by Third Schedule item, makes the violation a repeat violation` (`a violation by` `an individual violator` `of` `violation (6)` `on` (YMD 2028 6 1)) `an earlier item (5) violation on 16 March 2027, sanctioned`
-- Where the two readings agree: the same item.
#ASSERT     `s 45(b) — the previous violation, read by Third Schedule item, makes the violation a repeat violation` (`a violation by` `an individual violator` `of` `violation (1)` `on` (YMD 2028 6 1)) `an earlier item (1) violation on 16 March 2027, sanctioned`

-- The window with IL s.10(c) applied (F-WINDOW, the PLAN's kind W): 16 and 17 March 2029 are days of rest, so the
-- window ends on Sunday 18 March 2029.
#ASSERT `s 45(b) — the last day of the two years from the previous violation, when s 10(c) applies` `an earlier item (1) violation on 16 March 2027, sanctioned` `the Friday 16 and Saturday 17 March 2029 as days of rest` EQUALS YMD 2029 3 18
#ASSERT NOT `s 45(b) — the previous violation, with s 10(c) applied to the window, makes the violation a repeat violation` (`a violation by` `an individual violator` `of` `violation (1)` `on` (YMD 2029 3 19)) `an earlier item (1) violation on 16 March 2027, sanctioned` `the Friday 16 and Saturday 17 March 2029 as days of rest`
#ASSERT     `s 45(b) — the previous violation, with s 10(c) applied to the window, makes the violation a repeat violation` (`a violation by` `an individual violator` `of` `violation (1)` `on` (YMD 2029 3 18)) `an earlier item (1) violation on 16 March 2027, sanctioned` `the Friday 16 and Saturday 17 March 2029 as days of rest`
#ASSERT     `s 45(b) — the previous violation, with s 10(c) applied to the window, makes the violation a repeat violation` (`a violation by` `an individual violator` `of` `violation (1)` `on` (YMD 2029 3 17)) `an earlier item (1) violation on 16 March 2027, sanctioned` `the Friday 16 and Saturday 17 March 2029 as days of rest`

-- "an amount equal to the said financial sanction is added": the fixed sanction again, only if it is a repeat.
#ASSERT `s 45(b) — the addition for a repeat violation of` 20_000 `where` TRUE EQUALS 20_000
#ASSERT `s 45(b) — the addition for a repeat violation of` 20_000 `where` FALSE EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 45(b) — the addition for a repeat violation of` 40_000 `where` TRUE EQUALS 40_000

§§ `s 46: the floor is the whole of the amounts fixed (the fixed sanction plus the s.45 additions)`

#ASSERT     `s 46(a) — a sanction of` 10_000 `is not lower than the amounts fixed, which are` 10_000
#ASSERT NOT `s 46(a) — a sanction of` 9_999 `is not lower than the amounts fixed, which are` 10_000
#ASSERT     `s 46(a) — a sanction of` 20_000 `is not lower than the amounts fixed, which are` 10_000
-- Without regulations under s.46(b) the floor is the amounts fixed.
#ASSERT `s 46 — the lowest sanction the Commissioner may impose` 10_000 FALSE NOTHING EQUALS 10_000
-- With regulations that fix a rate of reduction of a fifth, the floor is four fifths.
#ASSERT `s 46 — the lowest sanction the Commissioner may impose` 10_000 TRUE (JUST 0.2) EQUALS 8_000
-- Reliance on regulations that the sources do not contain, with no rate supplied: the Law does not answer.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 46 — the lowest sanction the Commissioner may impose` 10_000 TRUE NOTHING BECAUSE "s 46(b) — no regulations fixing the circumstances and the rates for lower amounts are in the sources, so no lower floor can be computed"
-- A rate supplied but not relied on changes nothing.
#ASSERT `s 46 — the lowest sanction the Commissioner may impose` 10_000 FALSE (JUST 0.2) EQUALS 10_000

-- The prohibition: imposing 9,000 under a floor of 10,000 is a breach; imposing 10,000 is not the forbidden act.
#TRACE `s 46(a) — the Commissioner shall not impose a sanction below the floor of` 10_000 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `impose a financial sanction in this amount` `the Commissioner` 9_000 AT 5
#TRACE `s 46(a) — the Commissioner shall not impose a sanction below the floor of` 10_000 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `impose a financial sanction in this amount` `the Commissioner` 10_000 AT 5
-- The power to set lower amounts: consent and approval needed.
#TRACE `s 46(b) — the Minister may set the circumstances and rates for lower amounts` TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `prescribe by regulations the circumstances and rates for lower amounts` `the Minister` AT 1
#TRACE `s 46(b) — the Minister may set the circumstances and rates for lower amounts` TRUE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 1)

§§ `s 47(a): the day on which the amount is updated`

-- Representations made, the demand delivered on 1 June 2027, no stayed appeal: the demand's day.
#ASSERT `s 47(a) — the day on which the amount of the sanction is updated` (YMD 2027 3 3) TRUE (JUST (YMD 2027 6 1)) FALSE NOTHING EQUALS JUST (YMD 2027 6 1)
-- No representations (s.44(d)): the day the notice of intention was delivered, not the deemed demand's day.
#ASSERT `s 47(a) — the day on which the amount of the sanction is updated` (YMD 2027 3 3) FALSE (JUST (YMD 2027 4 2)) FALSE NOTHING EQUALS JUST (YMD 2027 3 3)
-- A stayed appeal: the day of the decision on the appeal, over both of the others.
#ASSERT `s 47(a) — the day on which the amount of the sanction is updated` (YMD 2027 3 3) TRUE (JUST (YMD 2027 6 1)) TRUE (JUST (YMD 2028 2 1)) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2028 2 1)
#ASSERT `s 47(a) — the day on which the amount of the sanction is updated` (YMD 2027 3 3) FALSE (JUST (YMD 2027 4 2)) TRUE (JUST (YMD 2028 2 1)) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2028 2 1)
-- Appeal stayed but not yet decided: there is no such day yet.
#ASSERT `s 47(a) — the day on which the amount of the sanction is updated` (YMD 2027 3 3) TRUE (JUST (YMD 2027 6 1)) TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- Representations made but no demand yet and no appeal: no day yet.
#ASSERT `s 47(a) — the day on which the amount of the sanction is updated` (YMD 2027 3 3) TRUE NOTHING FALSE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- The alternative order (F-DAY) differs only for a violator who made no representations and whose stayed appeal was decided.
#ASSERT `s 47(a) — the day on which the amount of the sanction is updated, the demand's day before the appeal's` (YMD 2027 3 3) FALSE (JUST (YMD 2027 4 2)) TRUE (JUST (YMD 2028 2 1)) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2027 3 3)
#ASSERT `s 47(a) — the day on which the amount of the sanction is updated, the demand's day before the appeal's` (YMD 2027 3 3) TRUE (JUST (YMD 2027 6 1)) TRUE (JUST (YMD 2028 2 1)) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2028 2 1)

§§ `s 47(b): the index known on a day, rounding, and the yearly chain`

-- A reading published ON a day is known on it; the latest month among those published wins.
#ASSERT `s 47(b) — the index known on` (YMD 2025 1 1) `among` `the index readings` EQUALS 100.0
#ASSERT `s 47(b) — the index known on` (YMD 2025 1 14) `among` `the index readings` EQUALS 100.0
#ASSERT `s 47(b) — the index known on` (YMD 2025 1 15) `among` `the index readings` EQUALS 100.4
#ASSERT `s 47(b) — the index known on` (YMD 2026 1 1) `among` `the index readings` EQUALS 101.7
#ASSERT `s 47(b) — the index known on` (YMD 2027 1 1) `among` `the index readings` EQUALS 103.4
#ASSERT `s 47(b) — the index known on` (YMD 2024 11 15) `among` `the index readings` EQUALS 99.8
-- Nothing published yet: the Law does not give it.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 47(b) — the index known on` (YMD 2024 11 14) `among` `the index readings` BECAUSE "s 47(b) — no reading of the index had been published on that day, so the index known on it is not given"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 47(b) — the index known on` (YMD 2026 1 1) `among` EMPTY BECAUSE "s 47(b) — no reading of the index had been published on that day, so the index known on it is not given"

-- Rounding to the nearest multiple of NIS 10.
#ASSERT `s 47(b) — the nearest multiple of NIS 10 to` 20_340 EQUALS 20_340
#ASSERT `s 47(b) — the nearest multiple of NIS 10 to` 3_051 EQUALS 3_050
#ASSERT `s 47(b) — the nearest multiple of NIS 10 to` 3_054 EQUALS 3_050
#ASSERT `s 47(b) — the nearest multiple of NIS 10 to` 3_056 EQUALS 3_060
#ASSERT `s 47(b) — the nearest multiple of NIS 10 to` 3_059 EQUALS 3_060
-- Exactly half-way: half up (taken) and half to even (F-ROUND).
#ASSERT `s 47(b) — the nearest multiple of NIS 10 to` 5_085 EQUALS 5_090
#ASSERT `s 47(b) — the nearest multiple of NIS 10, a half going to the even multiple, to` 5_085 EQUALS 5_080
#ASSERT `s 47(b) — the nearest multiple of NIS 10 to` 5_095 EQUALS 5_100
#ASSERT `s 47(b) — the nearest multiple of NIS 10, a half going to the even multiple, to` 5_095 EQUALS 5_100

-- The amount on a day, the first update being on 1 January 2026.
-- Before the first update the amount is as enacted; 1 January itself is an update day.
#ASSERT `s 47(b) — the amount of` 20_000 `updated on` (YMD 2025 12 31) `, the first update being in` 2026 `and the index readings being` `the index readings` EQUALS 20_000
#ASSERT `s 47(b) — the amount of` 20_000 `updated on` (YMD 2026 1 1) `, the first update being in` 2026 `and the index readings being` `the index readings` EQUALS 20_340
#ASSERT `s 47(b) — the amount of` 20_000 `updated on` (YMD 2026 12 31) `, the first update being in` 2026 `and the index readings being` `the index readings` EQUALS 20_340
#ASSERT `s 47(b) — the amount of` 20_000 `updated on` (YMD 2027 1 1) `, the first update being in` 2026 `and the index readings being` `the index readings` EQUALS 20_680
#ASSERT `s 47(b) — the amount of` 20_000 `updated on` (YMD 2027 12 31) `, the first update being in` 2026 `and the index readings being` `the index readings` EQUALS 20_680
-- The other items of the Third Schedule, individual column.
#ASSERT `s 47(b) — the amount of` 10_000 `updated on` (YMD 2026 6 1) `, the first update being in` 2026 `and the index readings being` `the index readings` EQUALS 10_170
#ASSERT `s 47(b) — the amount of` 3_000 `updated on` (YMD 2026 6 1) `, the first update being in` 2026 `and the index readings being` `the index readings` EQUALS 3_050
#ASSERT `s 47(b) — the amount of` 6_000 `updated on` (YMD 2026 6 1) `, the first update being in` 2026 `and the index readings being` `the index readings` EQUALS 6_100
#ASSERT `s 47(b) — the amount of` 40_000 `updated on` (YMD 2026 6 1) `, the first update being in` 2026 `and the index readings being` `the index readings` EQUALS 40_680
#ASSERT `s 47(b) — the amount of` 40_000 `updated on` (YMD 2027 6 1) `, the first update being in` 2026 `and the index readings being` `the index readings` EQUALS 41_360
-- NIS 5,000 is half-way after the first update: 5,085 rounds to 5,090 (taken).
#ASSERT `s 47(b) — the amount of` 5_000 `updated on` (YMD 2026 6 1) `, the first update being in` 2026 `and the index readings being` `the index readings` EQUALS 5_090
-- The chain (F-CHAIN): each year's rounded amount is the next year's base, so 5,090 goes on to 5,180 ...
#ASSERT `s 47(b) — the amount of` 5_000 `updated on` (YMD 2027 6 1) `, the first update being in` 2026 `and the index readings being` `the index readings` EQUALS 5_180
-- ... where rounding once at the end gives 5,170.
#ASSERT `s 47(b) — the amount of` 5_000 `updated on` (YMD 2027 6 1) `, rounded once at the end, the first update being in` 2026 `and the index readings being` `the index readings` EQUALS 5_170
-- Where there is no difference: 20,000 gives 20,680 either way.
#ASSERT `s 47(b) — the amount of` 20_000 `updated on` (YMD 2027 6 1) `, rounded once at the end, the first update being in` 2026 `and the index readings being` `the index readings` EQUALS 20_680
-- The first update in 2025 would need the index known on 1 January 2024, which the readings do not have.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 47(b) — the amount of` 20_000 `updated on` (YMD 2025 3 1) `, the first update being in` 2025 `and the index readings being` `the index readings`

§§ `ss 45 to 47 together: the financial sanction for a violation`

-- No update yet (the day is before 2026), no continuation, no repeat: the amount column B fixes.
#ASSERT `s 45 to 47 — the financial sanction for the violation` (`a violation by` `an individual violator` `of` `violation (5)` `on` (YMD 2027 3 1)) 0 FALSE (YMD 2025 12 31) 2026 `the index readings` EQUALS 20_000
#ASSERT `s 45 to 47 — the financial sanction for the violation` (`a violation by` `an individual violator` `of` `violation (1)` `on` (YMD 2027 3 1)) 0 FALSE (YMD 2025 12 31) 2026 `the index readings` EQUALS 20_000
#ASSERT `s 45 to 47 — the financial sanction for the violation` (`a violation by` `an individual violator` `of` `violation (7)` `on` (YMD 2027 3 1)) 0 FALSE (YMD 2025 12 31) 2026 `the index readings` EQUALS 3_000
#ASSERT `s 45 to 47 — the financial sanction for the violation` (`a violation by` `a corporate violator` `of` `violation (7)` `on` (YMD 2027 3 1)) 0 FALSE (YMD 2025 12 31) 2026 `the index readings` EQUALS 6_000
-- A corporation at a dash: the Law does not answer, never 0 and never the individual amount.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 45 to 47 — the financial sanction for the violation` (`a violation by` `a corporate violator` `of` `violation (1)` `on` (YMD 2027 3 1)) 0 FALSE (YMD 2025 12 31) 2026 `the index readings`
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 45 to 47 — the financial sanction for the violation` (`a violation by` `a corporate violator` `of` `violation (4)` `on` (YMD 2027 3 1)) 3 TRUE (YMD 2027 6 1) 2026 `the index readings`
-- The continuing violation: 20,000 + 2 x 400 (months completed, 15 March to 14 June 2027), and with the other counts.
#ASSERT `s 45 to 47 — the financial sanction for the violation` (`a violation by` `an individual violator` `of` `violation (1)` `on` (YMD 2027 3 15)) (`s 45(a) — the whole months a violation continued from` (YMD 2027 3 15) `to` (YMD 2027 6 14)) FALSE (YMD 2025 12 31) 2026 `the index readings` EQUALS 20_800
#ASSERT `s 45 to 47 — the financial sanction for the violation` (`a violation by` `an individual violator` `of` `violation (1)` `on` (YMD 2027 3 15)) (`s 45(a) — the calendar months touched by a violation from` (YMD 2027 3 15) `to` (YMD 2027 6 14)) FALSE (YMD 2025 12 31) 2026 `the index readings` EQUALS 21_600
#ASSERT `s 45 to 47 — the financial sanction for the violation` (`a violation by` `an individual violator` `of` `violation (1)` `on` (YMD 2027 3 15)) (`s 45(a) — the calendar months touched after the first, by a violation from` (YMD 2027 3 15) `to` (YMD 2027 6 14)) FALSE (YMD 2025 12 31) 2026 `the index readings` EQUALS 21_200
-- The repeat violation doubles the fixed sanction: 20,000 + 20,000.
#ASSERT `s 45 to 47 — the financial sanction for the violation` (`a violation by` `an individual violator` `of` `violation (5)` `on` (YMD 2027 3 1)) 0 TRUE (YMD 2025 12 31) 2026 `the index readings` EQUALS 40_000
-- Trap T15: the cap of s.41(b) bounds what an ORDER may set, not what is payable.  Item (5) for a corporation
-- is 40,000, and 40,000 more for a repeat is 80,000 (the cap exactly); six months of continuation add 6 x 800.
#ASSERT `s 45 to 47 — the financial sanction for the violation` (`a violation by` `a corporate violator` `of` `violation (5)` `on` (YMD 2027 3 1)) 0 TRUE (YMD 2025 12 31) 2026 `the index readings` EQUALS 80_000
#ASSERT `s 45 to 47 — the financial sanction for the violation` (`a violation by` `a corporate violator` `of` `violation (5)` `on` (YMD 2027 3 1)) 6 TRUE (YMD 2025 12 31) 2026 `the index readings` EQUALS 84_800
#ASSERT 84_800 GREATER THAN `s 41(b) — the cap on a column B amount for` `a corporation`
-- ... and an update takes the fixed amount past the cap too: 40,680 x 2.
#ASSERT `s 45 to 47 — the financial sanction for the violation` (`a violation by` `a corporate violator` `of` `violation (5)` `on` (YMD 2027 3 1)) 0 TRUE (YMD 2026 3 1) 2026 `the index readings` EQUALS 81_360
-- With the update: item (3) for an individual is 5,090 on 1 June 2026, and 2 months add 2 x 5,090 / 50 = 203.6.
#ASSERT `s 45 to 47 — the financial sanction for the violation` (`a violation by` `an individual violator` `of` `violation (3)` `on` (YMD 2026 3 1)) 2 FALSE (YMD 2026 6 1) 2026 `the index readings` EQUALS 5_293.6
-- The alternative base (F-BASE): the additions on the enacted 5,000 (5,200), then updated and rounded once: 5,288.4 -> 5,290.
#ASSERT `s 45 to 47 — the financial sanction for the violation, with the additions computed on the amount as enacted` (`a violation by` `an individual violator` `of` `violation (3)` `on` (YMD 2026 3 1)) 2 FALSE (YMD 2026 6 1) 2026 `the index readings` EQUALS 5_290
-- Where the two bases agree: nothing added.
#ASSERT `s 45 to 47 — the financial sanction for the violation, with the additions computed on the amount as enacted` (`a violation by` `an individual violator` `of` `violation (1)` `on` (YMD 2026 3 1)) 0 FALSE (YMD 2026 6 1) 2026 `the index readings` EQUALS 20_340
-- A day on which the index cannot be read (the first update in 2025, with no reading before 15 November 2024): refused.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 45 to 47 — the financial sanction for the violation` (`a violation by` `an individual violator` `of` `violation (1)` `on` (YMD 2027 3 1)) 0 FALSE (YMD 2025 3 1) 2025 `the index readings`

