    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)

§§ `Fork F-CAP (trap T15): the alternative that the cap of s 41(b) also bounds what is payable`

-- Corporation, item (5), repeat, six months: 84,800 payable; held to the cap it would be 80,000.
#ASSERT `s 45 to 47 — the financial sanction for the violation, held to the cap of s 41(b)` (`a violation by` `a corporate violator` `of` `violation (5)` `on` (YMD 2027 3 1)) 6 TRUE (YMD 2025 12 31) 2026 `the index readings` EQUALS 80_000
-- Individual, item (5), repeat: 40,000 is exactly the cap; one month more, 40,400, is held to 40,000.
#ASSERT `s 45 to 47 — the financial sanction for the violation, held to the cap of s 41(b)` (`a violation by` `an individual violator` `of` `violation (5)` `on` (YMD 2027 3 1)) 0 TRUE (YMD 2025 12 31) 2026 `the index readings` EQUALS 40_000
#ASSERT `s 45 to 47 — the financial sanction for the violation, held to the cap of s 41(b)` (`a violation by` `an individual violator` `of` `violation (5)` `on` (YMD 2027 3 1)) 1 TRUE (YMD 2025 12 31) 2026 `the index readings` EQUALS 40_000
#ASSERT `s 45 to 47 — the financial sanction for the violation, held to the cap of s 41(b)` (`a violation by` `an individual violator` `of` `violation (5)` `on` (YMD 2027 3 1)) 1 TRUE (YMD 2025 12 31) 2026 `the index readings` GREATER THAN 0
-- Under the cap, nothing changes.
#ASSERT `s 45 to 47 — the financial sanction for the violation, held to the cap of s 41(b)` (`a violation by` `an individual violator` `of` `violation (3)` `on` (YMD 2027 3 1)) 0 FALSE (YMD 2025 12 31) 2026 `the index readings` EQUALS 5_000
-- The reading taken for the same facts (item (5), individual, repeat, one month): 20,000 + 400 + 20,000 = 40,400.
#ASSERT `s 45 to 47 — the financial sanction for the violation` (`a violation by` `an individual violator` `of` `violation (5)` `on` (YMD 2027 3 1)) 1 TRUE (YMD 2025 12 31) 2026 `the index readings` EQUALS 40_400

