§§ `Fork F-R: the update day is 1 January even when it is a day of rest (kind R); the alternative moves it`

`Friday 1 and Saturday 2 January 2027 as days of rest` MEANS `Calendar of rest days` WITH `days of rest, recess or holiday` IS LIST (YMD 2027 1 1), (YMD 2027 1 2)
`no day of rest at all` MEANS `Calendar of rest days` WITH `days of rest, recess or holiday` IS EMPTY

#ASSERT `s 47(b) — the update day of` 2027 `if s 10(c) moved it past days of rest, with` `no day of rest at all` EQUALS YMD 2027 1 1
#ASSERT `s 47(b) — the update day of` 2027 `if s 10(c) moved it past days of rest, with` `Friday 1 and Saturday 2 January 2027 as days of rest` EQUALS YMD 2027 1 3
-- The reading taken: the amount is updated from 1 January itself, whatever the day is.
#ASSERT `s 47(b) — the amount of` 20_000 `updated on` (YMD 2027 1 1) `, the first update being in` 2026 `and the index readings being` `the index readings` EQUALS 20_680
#ASSERT `s 47(b) — the amount of` 20_000 `updated on` (YMD 2027 1 2) `, the first update being in` 2026 `and the index readings being` `the index readings` EQUALS 20_680

§§ `Trap T16, s 47(a) with s 44(d): a violator who made no representations is updated at the day of the notice, not the deemed demand`

-- Notice delivered 20 December 2026; the s.43 period ends 19 January 2027 (no rest days) and the notice is treated as a demand
